# core/models - Which models are loaded, and in which notation?
#
# Answers: every model resource, the metamodel it conforms to, its source file,
# and when it was converted.
#
# Does NOT prove: that a model is current. A conversion timestamp says when the
# RDF was produced, not when the architecture was last true.
#
# Run this with core/inventory during orientation. arch:modelConformsToMetamodel
# is the reliable way to tell which notations a dataset contains - far more so
# than inspecting element types, and more so than parsing IRIs, since the
# notation segment is configurable per converter.
#
# The model resource is read through the `model` GRAPH ROLE rather than the
# semantic one, because the converters moved it. At default pre-1.3 flags the
# model is declared in the semantic graph and the profile binds `model` to that
# same suffix; in the 1.3 layout it lives in `graph/model` and the profile binds it
# there. Asking for the role instead of naming a graph is what lets this template
# serve both generations unchanged - and the field report's "core/models returns 0
# rows" was exactly this template reading the wrong graph.
#
# Its provenance lives in the provenance graph either way, so this reaches across
# both. That is why ?source and ?generated are OPTIONAL: a model with no
# provenance graph still appears, which is itself worth seeing.
#
# Each provenance field is its own OPTIONAL carrying its own triple pattern and its
# own graph scope. Grouping them as OPTIONALs inside one GRAPH block reads better and
# is a trap: a group of nothing but OPTIONALs matches any graph trivially, leaving
# ?model unbound in that solution, which is compatible with every row and duplicates
# the result once per provenance graph in the dataset. Every fixture graph happens to
# carry a model-level triple, which is the only reason that shape survived here -
# core/resolve-model hit it for real.
#
# Parameters: LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT ?model ?metamodel ?title ?source ?generated
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:model}}
    ?model a {{ROLE:model_class}} .
    OPTIONAL { ?model {{ROLE:conforms_to_metamodel}} ?metamodel }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  OPTIONAL { {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}} ?model dct:title ?title {{GRAPH_CLOSE}} }
  OPTIONAL { {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance2}} ?model {{ROLE:source_file}} ?source {{GRAPH_CLOSE}} }
  OPTIONAL { {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance3}} ?model {{ROLE:generated_at}} ?generated {{GRAPH_CLOSE}} }
}
ORDER BY ?model
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
